{
  "slug": "baked-salmon-with-lemon-and-dill",
  "title": "Baked Salmon with Lemon and Dill",
  "blurb": "Salmon fillets baked with fresh lemon juice, white wine and cherry tomatoes, finished with chopped dill.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 180°C and lightly oil a baking dish large enough to hold the salmon fillets in a single layer.",
    "Place the salmon fillets skin-side down in the dish and season with salt and pepper.",
    "Halve the cherry tomatoes and scatter them around the salmon.",
    "Squeeze the lemon juice over the fish and tomatoes, then pour the white wine into the dish.",
    "Drizzle the olive oil over everything and place in the oven for 35 to 40 minutes until the salmon is cooked through.",
    "Finely chop the dill and scatter it over the salmon just before serving."
  ],
